{
  "borough": "London Borough of Barking and Dagenham",
  "application_type": "All Other",
  "decision": "Refused",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "The proposed development, by virtue of its design and siting, would present an&nbsp;inappropriate development&nbsp;that would disrupt the established pattern of dwellings with direct street frontages and organised building lines and would fail to adhere to existing building lines. It would have a poor street presence and would conflict with the existing planned form of development. As such, the proposal would appear incongruous and discordant, causing harm to the visual amenity and spatial character of the area, contrary to:National Planning Policy Framework (NPPF) (December 2024)Policy D4 of the London Plan (March 2021)Policies SP2, DMD1 and DMD4 of the Barking and Dagenham Local Plan (September 2024)",
    "The proposed development fails to provide clarity that additional demand for parking could be adequately accommodated, or that access of the existing dropped kerb for both properties can be accessed interchangeably and independently from each property. It has not been clarified that additional demand for parking from the development could be adequately accommodated in the surrounding area. Officers are unable to determine whether the proposal would result in parking stress and congestion in the vicinity of the application site.&nbsp; As such, it fails to comply with the following policies:National Planning Policy Framework (NPPF) (December 2024)Policies T1 and T6.1 of the London Plan (March 2021)Policy DMT2 of the Barking and Dagenham Local Plan (September 2024)"
  ],
